, paired-comparison, A/B, and split-cell designs are not appropriate. Policy priorities will be measured through balanced prioritisation questions after the pain-point diagnosis; a full MaxDiff exercise is not required at this stage because the study must first establish whether the proposed policy list reflects respondents’ real needs."],"\n",["P",{},"Alternatives considered:"],"\n",["UL",{},"\n",["LI",{},["STRONG",{},"Qualitative interviews:"]," Not selected as the primary design because interviews would provide depth but not a comparable prioritised view across work models and parent groups."],"\n",["LI",{},["STRONG",{},"MaxDiff / Best-Worst Scaling:"]," Not selected because the immediate decision is to diagnose the full pain-point lands"],"\n"]],[[28,513]]]]]],[[32,568]],[[32,569]]]]]]]],[[232,75]],[[522,191]]]]]],[[32,592]]]]]]]]]],[[538,507]],[[538,508]],[[538,509]]],[[538,656]],[[504,178]],[[522,236]],[[504,179]],[[134,599]],[[32,602]]]],"viewport":{"width":1280,"height":720},"timestamp":318358.637,"wallTime":1786695450383,"collectionTime":3.2999999821186066,"resourceOverrides":[],"isMainFrame":true}}
