{"type":"frame-snapshot","snapshot":{"callId":"call@738","snapshotName":"after@call@738","pageId":"page@11645576cb78270f3c1b6d7747f4c556","frameId":"frame@7aa660cb489ba03d3207f9a2a1977970","frameUrl":"https://dev.hercules.works/ai/chat/3d8e21ef-ce02-415d-9269-bef93fb1ce61","doctype":"html","html":["HTML",{"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","class":"scrollbar-hide","data-scroll-behavior":"smooth","style":""},[[575,31]],["BODY",{"class":"inter_ad991c7-module__LhgUwq__className inter_ad991c7-module__LhgUwq__variable roboto_20913b7b-module__RNtCNq__variable jetbrains_mono_68d574a-module__ggYvfa__variable","style":"overflow: unset;"},[[575,32]],[[609,90]],["DIV",{"id":"main-content"},["DIV",{},["DIV",{"class":"flex w-full bg-white flex-col h-[100dvh] overflow-hidden overflow-x-clip relative z-[11]","style":"opacity: 1; transform: none;"},[[593,45]],["DIV",{"class":"flex w-full bg-white flex-col flex-1 min-h-0 overflow-hidden overflow-x-clip relative z-[11]"},["MAIN",{"id":"main-content","class":"flex flex-1 min-h-0 overflow-y-auto overflow-x-clip relative w-full justify-end items-end "},[[575,42]],["DIV",{"class":"h-full relative min-w-0 p-0 ","style":"width: 1235px; height: 720px; transition: width 300ms ease-in-out;"},["DIV",{"class":"flex w-full h-full overflow-hidden relative"},["DIV",{"class":"h-full flex overflow-visible","style":"width: 100%; transition: width 300ms ease-in-out;"},["DIV",{"class":"relative w-full flex flex-col items-center mx-0 md:mx-[2%] h-full min-h-0 overflow-hidden justify-between"},["DIV",{"class":" flex-1   w-[95%] md:w-full min-h-0 mb-0 md:-mb-20 flex justify-center"},["DIV",{"class":"w-full md:w-[90%] flex flex-col z-[0] flex-1 min-h-0 overflow-x-hidden items-center"},["DIV",{"__playwright_scroll_top_":"12810","class":"flex justify-center min-h-0 w-[96%]  overflow-y-auto overflow-x-hidden scrollbar-hide z-10 items-center pt-4 "},["DIV",{"class":"w-full md:max-w-[820px] h-full"},[[593,139]],[[7,0]],["DIV",{"class":"flex justify-start pointer-events-auto  w-full"},["DIV",{"class":"flex flex-col w-[96%] mx-[2%]"},[[575,43]],["DIV",{"class":"flex w-full "},["DIV",{"class":"flex rounded-[8px] bg-transparent text-[#464646] w-full flex-shrink-0  mt-2"},["DIV",{"class":"flex flex-col w-full"},[[575,75]],["DIV",{"class":"flex flex-col w-full overflow-x-visible"},[[575,79]],["DIV",{"class":"flex w-full justify-start items-start flex-col mt-[8px] h-[24px] relative overflow-visible","style":"opacity: 1; transform: none;"},["DIV",{"class":"absolute inset-0 flex flex-col justify-between items-start pointer-events-none","style":"opacity: 1;"},["DIV",{"class":"flex items-center gap-[4px] -ml-[5px] pointer-events-auto"},[[575,81]],["BUTTON",{"class":"relative group flex items-center justify-center w-[24px] h-[24px] rounded-[8px] overflow-visible opacity-40 cursor-not-allowed","disabled":""},["SPAN",{"aria-hidden":"true","class":"flex-shrink-0 bg-[#808080] transition-colors duration-200 ","style":"width: 14px; height: 14px; mask-image: url(\"/icons/retry_2.svg\"); mask-size: contain; mask-repeat: no-repeat; mask-position: center center;"}]]]]],[[575,87]]]]]]]],[[7,12]],["DIV",{"class":"flex justify-start pointer-events-auto  w-full"},["DIV",{"class":"flex flex-col w-[96%] mx-[2%]"},[[205,11]],["DIV",{"class":"flex w-full "},["DIV",{"class":"flex rounded-[8px] bg-transparent text-[#464646] w-full flex-shrink-0  mt-2"},["DIV",{"class":"flex flex-col w-full"},["DIV",{"class":"mb-8 pointer-events-auto"},["DIV",{"class":"w-full max-w-[800px] mt-[12px]"},[[205,13]],[[205,22]],["DIV",{"class":"grid transition-[grid-template-rows] duration-300 ease-out","style":"grid-template-rows: 1fr;"},["DIV",{"class":"overflow-hidden min-w-0"},["DIV",{"class":"ml-[16px] mt-4 mb-[10px] min-w-0"},["DIV",{"class":"flex flex-col min-w-0"},[[205,37]],[[205,52]],["DIV",{"class":"flex gap-[8px] min-w-0"},[[205,56]],["DIV",{"class":"min-w-0 flex-1 "},[[205,59]],["DIV",{"class":"grid transition-[grid-template-rows] duration-300 ease-out","style":"grid-template-rows: 1fr;"},["DIV",{"class":"overflow-hidden min-w-0"},["DIV",{"class":"pt-[6px] allow-text-select"},["DIV",{"class":"min-w-0 max-w-full break-words"},["DIV",{"class":"roboto_9f186078-module__bqURWG__className mt-3 min-w-0 max-w-full break-words text-[12px] text-[#464646] leading-[160%]"},["H3",{"class":"text-[12px] font-bold text-[#464646] mt-4 mb-2","node":"[object Object]"},"Core Objective & Business Context"],[[205,62]],["P",{"class":"mb-3","node":"[object Object]"},"This study will identify the most important workplace pain points experienced by expecting parents and parents of young children across remote, hybrid, and office-based work arrangements. The goal is to translate those pain points into clear priorities for employer support, workplace policies, manager practices, and benefits."],[[205,65]],["P",{"class":"mb-3","node":"[object Object]"},"The timing is important because employers are balancing return-to-office expectations with employee demands for flexibility, while parents are managing childcare, interruptions, work-hour boundaries, performance visibility, and career progression. The research must distinguish between problems caused by the work location itself and problems caused by inflexible norms, poor manager support, or insufficient benefits."],[[205,68]],["P",{"class":"mb-3","node":"[object Object]"},"Knowing the answers will help employers decide which interventions to prioritise first, such as flexible hours, predictable meeting norms, childcare support, manager training, phased return-to-work policies, equipment support, or career-protection measures."],[[205,71]],["H3",{"class":"text-[12px] font-bold text-[#464646] mt-4 mb-2","node":"[object Object]"},"Secondary Research Snapshot"],[[205,74]],["UL",{"class":"list-disc pl-5 mb-3 flex flex-col gap-1","node":"[object Object]"},"\n",["LI",{"class":"leading-[150%]","node":"[object Object]"},"\n",["P",{"class":"mb-3","node":"[object Object]"},["STRONG",{"class":"font-bold text-[#464646]","node":"[object Object]"},"Hybrid work is currently preferred by many Indian employees, but actual working patterns lag behind preference."]," ACCA’s India Talent Trends 2026 reports that 79% of respondents prefer hybrid work, while 53% are already working in a hybrid model. This supports comparing preferred and current arrangements rather than measuring preference alone. (",["A",{"class":"text-[#1A73E8] hover:underline","href":"https://www.dev.accaglobal.com/content/dam/ACCA_Global/professional-insights/GTT-2026/gtt-india-2026-final.pdf","node":"[object Object]"},"dev.accaglobal.com"],")"],"\n"],"\n",["LI",{"class":"leading-[150%]","node":"[object Object]"},"\n",["P",{"class":"mb-3","node":"[object Object]"},["STRONG",{"class":"font-bold text-[#464646]","node":"[object Object]"},"Flexibility is linked to more than location."]," ACCA’s India Talent Trends 2025 found that work-life balance, commuting time and cost, and schedule flexibility were key perceived benefits of working from home. The survey should therefore measure control over working hours and predictability, not just remote versus office status. (",["A",{"class":"text-[#1A73E8] hover:underline","href":"http://www.accaglobal.com/content/dam/ACCA_Global/professional-insights/Global-talent-trends-2025/PI-GTT-2025-INDIA%20v4.pdf","node":"[object Object]"},"accaglobal.com"],")"],"\n"],"\n",["LI",{"class":"leading-[150%]","node":"[object Object]"},"\n",["P",{"class":"mb-3","node":"[object Object]"},["STRONG",{"class":"font-bold text-[#464646]","node":"[object Object]"},"Office attendance does not resolve the broader employee experience."]," JLL’s 2025 India workplace research highlights that employees increasingly expect employers to address well-being, purpose, and personal circumstances alongside physical workplace quality. This supports testing policy and manager behaviours as separate support levers. (",["A",{"class":"text-[#1A73E8] hover:underline","href":"https://www.jll.com/en-in/insights/beyond-mandates-the-future-of-work-in-india","node":"[object Object]"},"jll.com"],", ",["A",{"class":"text-[#1A73E8] hover:underline","href":"https://www.jll.com/en-sa/insights/workforce-preference-barometer","node":"[object Object]"},"jll.com"],")"],"\n"],"\n",["LI",{"class":"leading-[150%]","node":"[object Object]"},"\n",["P",{"class":"mb-3","node":"[object Object]"},["STRONG",{"class":"font-bold text-[#464646]","node":"[object Object]"},"Care work is a significant structural issue in India."]," UNDP reports that unpaid care and domestic work in India represent an estimated 15%–17% of GDP, while women continue to carry a disproportionate share of unpaid care work. The questionnaire should allow analysis by parent gender without assuming that all parents experience care responsibilities in the same way. (",["A",{"class":"text-[#1A73E8] hover:underline","href":"https://www.undp.org/sites/g/files/zskgke326/files/2024-12/undp_brochure_care_project.pdf","node":"[object Object]"},"undp.org"],", ",["A",{"class":"text-[#1A73E8] hover:underline","href":"https://www.undp.org/india/blog/who-cares-making-care-everyones-work","node":"[object Object]"},"undp.org"],")"],"\n"],"\n",["LI",{"class":"leading-[150%]","node":"[object Object]"},"\n",["P",{"class":"mb-3","node":"[object Object]"},["STRONG",{"class":"font-bold text-[#464646]","node":"[object Object]"},"The key research gap is parent-specific evidence."]," Existing workplace studies generally report overall employee preferences. This study should identify which workplace barriers are uniquely severe for expecting parents and parents of young children, and which employer actions are perceived as practical and credible by this audience."],"\n"],"\n"],[[205,135]],["H3",{"class":"text-[12px] font-bold text-[#464646] mt-4 mb-2","node":"[object Object]"},"Research Type & Methodology"],[[205,138]],["UL",{"class":"list-disc pl-5 mb-3 flex flex-col gap-1","node":"[object Object]"},"\n",["LI",{"class":"leading-[150%]","node":"[object Object]"},"\n",["P",{"class":"mb-3","node":"[object Object]"},["STRONG",{"class":"font-bold text-[#464646]","node":"[object Object]"},"Study type:"]," Employee / Internal Research combined with Usage & Attitude and policy-prioritisation research."],"\n"],"\n",["LI",{"class":"leading-[150%]","node":"[object Object]"},"\n",["P",{"class":"mb-3","node":"[object Object]"},["STRONG",{"class":"font-bold text-[#464646]","node":"[object Object]"},"Stimulus count:"]," Zero discrete stimuli. The study is not evaluating products, advertisements, concepts, packages, or variants. Cell-based designs such as monadic, A/B, paired comparison, and sequential monadic testing do not apply."],"\n"],"\n",["LI",{"class":"leading-[150%]","node":"[object Object]"},"\n",["P",{"class":"mb-3","node":"[object Object]"},["STRONG",{"class":"font-bold text-[#464646]","node":"[object Object]"},"Research design:"]," Linear structured questionnaire using a modular funnel. The survey will move from current work arrangement and recent experiences to pain points, support needs, policy priorities, and recommended actions."],"\n"],"\n",["LI",{"class":"leading-[150%]","node":"[object Object]"},"\n",["P",{"class":"mb-3","node":"[object Object]"},["STRONG",{"class":"font-bold text-[#464646]","node":"[object Object]"},"Why this approach:"]," The business decision is about prioritising employer support, not selecting a winning creative or product option. A descriptive design will capture the lived experience of parents across remote, hybrid, and office-based settings while enabling meaningful subgroup comparisons by parent status, work model, and caregiving situation."],"\n"],"\n",["LI",{"class":"leading-[150%]","node":"[object Object]"},"\n",["P",{"class":"mb-3","node":"[object Object]"},["STRONG",{"class":"font-bold text-[#464646]","node":"[object Object]"},"Alternatives considered:"]],"\n",["UL",{"class":"list-disc pl-5 mb-3 flex flex-col gap-1","node":"[object Object]"},"\n",["LI",{"class":"leading-[150%]","node":"[object Object]"},["STRONG",{"class":"font-bold text-[#464646]","node":"[object Object]"},"Qualitative interviews:"]," Useful for deeper personal stories, but less suitable as the first step when the organisation needs a prioritised view across several work arrangements."],"\n",["LI",{"class":"leading-[150%]","node":"[object Object]"},["STRONG",{"class":"font-bold text-[#464646]","node":"[object Object]"},"MaxDiff prioritisation:"]," Could rank a predefined list of policies, but would be premature before understanding the full range of pain points and whether the policy list reflects respondents’ real needs."],"\n",["LI",{"class":"leading-[150%]","node":"[object Object]"},["STRONG",{"class":"font-bold text-[#464646]","node":"[object Object]"},"Conjoint or choice-based modelling:"]," Not chosen because the immediate decision is to diagnose problems and prioritise support areas, not model trade-offs between fully specified policy packages."],"\n"],"\n"],"\n",["LI",{"class":"leading-[150%]","node":"[object Object]"},"\n",["P",{"class":"mb-3","node":"[object Object]"},["STRONG",{"class":"font-bold text-[#464646]","node":"[object Object]"},"User control:"]," If you prefer a different methodology, such as adding qualitative interviews or a follow-up policy prioritisation exercise, it can be changed before the research brief is generated."],"\n"],"\n",["LI",{"class":"leading-[150%]","node":"[object Object]"},"\n",["P",{"class":"mb-3","node":"[object Object]"},["STRONG",{"class":"font-bold text-[#464646]","node":"[object Object]"},"Survey design logic:"]," Current behaviour will come before attitudes and policy preferences. The questionnaire will separate current work arrangement from preferred arrangement, ask about concrete recent situations before general satisfaction, and distinguish personal pain points from employer or manager-level causes. Parent groups will be compared without forcing a single definition of the “typical” new parent."],"\n"],"\n",["LI",{"class":"leading-[150%]","node":"[object Object]"},"\n",["P",{"class":"mb-3","node":"[object Object]"},["STRONG",{"class":"font-bold text-[#464646]","node":"[object Object]"},"Quality controls:"]," Include platform-compliant attention checks, speeder detection, straight-line response checks, duplicate or inconsistent answer screening, and open-ended gibberish review. Use short screens, fully labelled response scales, and minimal grids for SuperJ mobile and web respondents."],"\n"],"\n"],[[205,222]],["H3",{"class":"text-[12px] font-bold text-[#464646] mt-4 mb-2","node":"[object Object]"},"Target Audience Profile"],[[205,225]],["UL",{"class":"list-disc pl-5 mb-3 flex flex-col gap-1","node":"[object Object]"},"\n",["LI",{"class":"leading-[150%]","node":"[object Object]"},"\n",["P",{"class":"mb-3","node":"[object Object]"},["STRONG",{"class":"font-bold text-[#464646]","node":"[object Object]"},"Who we are asking:"]," Indian adults who are expecting a child, planning parental leave, or parenting a young child while currently working remotely, in a hybrid model, or mainly from an office."],"\n"],"\n",["LI",{"class":"leading-[150%]","node":"[object Object]"},"\n",["P",{"class":"mb-3","node":"[object Object]"},["STRONG",{"class":"font-bold text-[#464646]","node":"[object Object]"},"Why they matter:"]," These respondents are directly experiencing the interaction between caregiving demands and workplace expectations. Their answers can reveal whether flexibility is genuinely usable, whether managers respond constructively to interruptions, and whether workplace policies protect productivity, well-being, and career progression."],"\n"],"\n",["LI",{"class":"leading-[150%]","node":"[object Object]"},"\n",["P",{"class":"mb-3","node":"[object Object]"},["STRONG",{"class":"font-bold text-[#464646]","node":"[object Object]"},"Must-have screening criteria:"]],"\n",["UL",{"class":"list-disc pl-5 mb-3 flex flex-col gap-1","node":"[object Object]"},"\n",["LI",{"class":"leading-[150%]","node":"[object Object]"},"Currently employed or actively working in a paid role."],"\n",["LI",{"class":"leading-[150%]","node":"[object Object]"},"Expecting a child, planning parental leave, or caring for at least one young child."],"\n",["LI",{"class":"leading-[150%]","node":"[object Object]"},"Currently working remotely, in a hybrid model, or mainly from an office."],"\n",["LI",{"class":"leading-[150%]","node":"[object Object]"},"Able to describe their recent work and caregiving experience."],"\n",["LI",{"class":"leading-[150%]","node":"[object Object]"},"Capture whether the respondent is the primary caregiver, shares caregiving, or has another regular caregiving arrangement."],"\n"],"\n"],"\n",["LI",{"class":"leading-[150%]","node":"[object Object]"},"\n",["P",{"class":"mb-3","node":"[object Object]"},["STRONG",{"class":"font-bold text-[#464646]","node":"[object Object]"},"Important subgroup cuts:"]," Work arrangement, expecting parent versus parent of a young child, parent gender, primary versus shared caregiving responsibility, access to paid or family childcare, work seniority, and whether the employer currently offers formal support."],"\n"],"\n",["LI",{"class":"leading-[150%]","node":"[object Object]"},"\n",["P",{"class":"mb-3","node":"[object Object]"},["STRONG",{"class":"font-bold text-[#464646]","node":"[object Object]"},"Fielding context:"]," Respondents will be reached through verified Indian audiences on the SuperJ mobile application and web. Age, gender, city, and NCCS targeting should be enforced by the audience system before survey entry rather than recollected in the questionnaire."],"\n"],"\n"],[[205,285]],["H3",{"class":"text-[12px] font-bold text-[#464646] mt-4 mb-2","node":"[object Object]"},"Key Information Areas & Data Architecture"],[[205,288]],["UL",{"class":"list-disc pl-5 mb-3 flex flex-col gap-1","node":"[object Object]"},"\n",["LI",{"class":"leading-[150%]","node":"[object Object]"},"\n",["P",{"class":"mb-3","node":"[object Object]"},["STRONG",{"class":"font-bold text-[#464646]","node":"[object Object]"},"Current work arrangement and flexibility:"]," Capture actual work model, expected office attendance, control over start and finish times, and ability to adjust schedules. → Reveals whether the problem is location, schedule control, or both. → Drives recommendations on hybrid policy and flexible-hours design."],"\n"],"\n",["LI",{"class":"leading-[150%]","node":"[object Object]"},"\n",["P",{"class":"mb-3","node":"[object Object]"},["STRONG",{"class":"font-bold text-[#464646]","node":"[object Object]"},"Caregiving context:"]," Capture child age or pregnancy stage, caregiving role, childcare availability, and frequency of unexpected care interruptions. → Reveals which parent groups face the greatest operational pressure. → Drives targeted rather than one-size-fits-all support."],"\n"],"\n",["LI",{"class":"leading-[150%]","node":"[object Object]"},"\n",["P",{"class":"mb-3","node":"[object Object]"},["STRONG",{"class":"font-bold text-[#464646]","node":"[object Object]"},"Work-life boundaries:"]," Measure after-hours work, meeting spillover, inability to disconnect, schedule unpredictability, and pressure to remain continuously available. → Identifies boundary failures that may exist even in remote work. → Drives meeting, communication, and working-hours norms."],"\n"],"\n",["LI",{"class":"leading-[150%]","node":"[object Object]"},"\n",["P",{"class":"mb-3","node":"[object Object]"},["STRONG",{"class":"font-bold text-[#464646]","node":"[object Object]"},"Productivity and concentration:"]," Capture interruptions, suitable workspaces, concentration difficulty, technology limitations, and ability to complete focused work. → Separates environmental barriers from policy or management barriers. → Drives equipment, workspace, focus-time, and workload interventions."],"\n"],"\n",["LI",{"class":"leading-[150%]","node":"[object Object]"},"\n",["P",{"class":"mb-3","node":"[object Object]"},["STRONG",{"class":"font-bold text-[#464646]","node":"[object Object]"},"Manager and team expectations:"]," Measure comfort requesting flexibility, perceived response to interruptions, meeting culture, workload allocation, and psychological safety. → Shows whether formal policies are supported by day-to-day behaviour. → Drives manager training and accountability measures."],"\n"],"\n",["LI",{"class":"leading-[150%]","node":"[object Object]"},"\n",["P",{"class":"mb-3","node":"[object Object]"},["STRONG",{"class":"font-bold text-[#464646]","node":"[object Object]"},"Career growth and visibility:"]," Capture concerns about promotion, performance evaluation, access to important projects, networking, and visibility while working flexibly or taking leave. → Identifies longer-term career risks beyond immediate workload pain. → Drives return-to-work, performance-review, sponsorship, and progression policies."],"\n"],"\n",["LI",{"class":"leading-[150%]","node":"[object Object]"},"\n",["P",{"class":"mb-3","node":"[object Object]"},["STRONG",{"class":"font-bold text-[#464646]","node":"[object Object]"},"Employer support priorities:"]," Present a carefully balanced list of potential support actions after the pain-point diagnosis. → Reveals which interventions are both important and credible to parents. → Drives a prioritised employer action roadmap rather than a broad list of benefits."],"\n"],"\n"],[[205,347]],["H3",{"class":"text-[12px] font-bold text-[#464646] mt-4 mb-2","node":"[object Object]"},"Survey Flow & Question Design Approach"],[[205,350]],["UL",{"class":"list-disc pl-5 mb-3 flex flex-col gap-1","node":"[object Object]"},"\n",["LI",{"class":"leading-[150%]","node":"[object Object]"},"\n",["P",{"class":"mb-3","node":"[object Object]"},["STRONG",{"class":"font-bold text-[#464646]","node":"[object Object]"},"Phase 1 — Warm-up and eligibility:"]," Establish employment status, parent or expecting-parent status, current work model, and recent work recency. Use behavioural screening rather than asking only whether respondents “feel” like working parents."],"\n"],"\n",["LI",{"class":"leading-[150%]","node":"[object Object]"},"\n",["P",{"class":"mb-3","node":"[object Object]"},["STRONG",{"class":"font-bold text-[#464646]","node":"[object Object]"},"Phase 2 — Current working and caregiving context:"]," Capture work location, schedule control, childcare arrangements, caregiving role, leave status or plans, and typical points of overlap between work and care. This creates the context needed to interpret later pain-point ratings."],"\n"],"\n",["LI",{"class":"leading-[150%]","node":"[object Object]"},"\n",["P",{"class":"mb-3","node":"[object Object]"},["STRONG",{"class":"font-bold text-[#464646]","node":"[object Object]"},"Phase 3 — Pain-point diagnosis:"]," Measure the frequency and severity of childcare interruptions, work-hour boundary issues, concentration problems, manager expectations, technology or workspace barriers, and career visibility concerns. Use fully labelled 5-point scales and concrete time or occurrence anchors where possible."],"\n"],"\n",["LI",{"class":"leading-[150%]","node":"[object Object]"},"\n",["P",{"class":"mb-3","node":"[object Object]"},["STRONG",{"class":"font-bold text-[#464646]","node":"[object Object]"},"Phase 4 — Support and policy evaluation:"]," Explore which forms of employer support respondents currently receive, which are actually usable, and where the largest gap exists between support offered and support needed. Keep formal policy availability separate from awareness, access, and perceived usefulness."],"\n"],"\n",["LI",{"class":"leading-[150%]","node":"[object Object]"},"\n",["P",{"class":"mb-3","node":"[object Object]"},["STRONG",{"class":"font-bold text-[#464646]","node":"[object Object]"},"Phase 5 — Prioritisation and decision close:"]," Ask respondents to identify the most important employer action, the most urgent problem to solve, and the support that would have the greatest practical impact. Include a concise open-ended question for an example of a policy or manager behaviour that would make work easier."],"\n"],"\n",["LI",{"class":"leading-[150%]","node":"[object Object]"},"\n",["P",{"class":"mb-3","node":"[object Object]"},["STRONG",{"class":"font-bold text-[#464646]","node":"[object Object]"},"Phase 6 — Optional classification module:"]," Use existing audience targeting for age, gender, city, and NCCS. Only collect additional classification variables needed for analysis, such as seniority, employment type, caregiving arrangement, and access to childcare."],"\n"],"\n",["LI",{"class":"leading-[150%]","node":"[object Object]"},"\n",["P",{"class":"mb-3","node":"[object Object]"},["STRONG",{"class":"font-bold text-[#464646]","node":"[object Object]"},"Estimated length:"]," Approximately 15–25 questions and 8–12 minutes, with routing used to avoid asking expecting parents questions that apply only to parents already caring for a child."],"\n"],"\n"],[[205,409]],["H3",{"class":"text-[12px] font-bold text-[#464646] mt-4 mb-2","node":"[object Object]"},"Expected Insights & Business Decisions Enabled"],[[205,412]],["UL",{"class":"list-disc pl-5 mb-3 flex flex-col gap-1","node":"[object Object]"},"\n",["LI",{"class":"leading-[150%]","node":"[object Object]"},"\n",["P",{"class":"mb-3","node":"[object Object]"},["STRONG",{"class":"font-bold text-[#464646]","node":"[object Object]"},"You will be able to:"]," Identify the most frequent and severe pain points for expecting parents and parents of young children across remote, hybrid, and office-based work."],"\n"],"\n",["LI",{"class":"leading-[150%]","node":"[object Object]"},"\n",["P",{"class":"mb-3","node":"[object Object]"},["STRONG",{"class":"font-bold text-[#464646]","node":"[object Object]"},"You will be able to:"]," Separate problems caused by work location from problems caused by unpredictable schedules, team norms, manager behaviour, insufficient childcare support, or career anxiety."],"\n"],"\n",["LI",{"class":"leading-[150%]","node":"[object Object]"},"\n",["P",{"class":"mb-3","node":"[object Object]"},["STRONG",{"class":"font-bold text-[#464646]","node":"[object Object]"},"You will be able to:"]," Compare the gap between current work arrangements and preferred arrangements, including whether parents want fully remote work, structured hybrid work, greater schedule control, or better support within office-based work."],"\n"],"\n",["LI",{"class":"leading-[150%]","node":"[object Object]"},"\n",["P",{"class":"mb-3","node":"[object Object]"},["STRONG",{"class":"font-bold text-[#464646]","node":"[object Object]"},"You will be able to:"]," Identify which support needs differ between expecting parents, parents of infants, and parents of older young children."],"\n"],"\n",["LI",{"class":"leading-[150%]","node":"[object Object]"},"\n",["P",{"class":"mb-3","node":"[object Object]"},["STRONG",{"class":"font-bold text-[#464646]","node":"[object Object]"},"You will be able to decide:"]," Which employer policy changes should receive first priority, such as flexible start and finish times, predictable meeting windows, childcare assistance, phased return-to-work, additional leave, manager training, or equipment support."],"\n"],"\n",["LI",{"class":"leading-[150%]","node":"[object Object]"},"\n",["P",{"class":"mb-3","node":"[object Object]"},["STRONG",{"class":"font-bold text-[#464646]","node":"[object Object]"},"You will be able to decide:"]," Whether the primary intervention should be a formal policy change, stronger implementation of existing benefits, manager accountability, or improved communication and access."],"\n"],"\n",["LI",{"class":"leading-[150%]","node":"[object Object]"},"\n",["P",{"class":"mb-3","node":"[object Object]"},["STRONG",{"class":"font-bold text-[#464646]","node":"[object Object]"},"You will be able to decide:"]," Which workplace practices may be unintentionally damaging career visibility, promotion confidence, or access to important work for parents using flexible arrangements."],"\n"],"\n",["LI",{"class":"leading-[150%]","node":"[object Object]"},"\n",["P",{"class":"mb-3","node":"[object Object]"},["STRONG",{"class":"font-bold text-[#464646]","node":"[object Object]"},"Key hypotheses being tested:"]],"\n",["UL",{"class":"list-disc pl-5 mb-3 flex flex-col gap-1","node":"[object Object]"},"\n",["LI",{"class":"leading-[150%]","node":"[object Object]"},"Parents experience work-hour unpredictability and boundary erosion as major problems even when they work remotely."],"\n",["LI",{"class":"leading-[150%]","node":"[object Object]"},"Hybrid work is valuable only when office attendance is predictable and compatible with caregiving arrangements."],"\n",["LI",{"class":"leading-[150%]","node":"[object Object]"},"Manager response and team norms may matter more than the formal availability of flexibility."],"\n",["LI",{"class":"leading-[150%]","node":"[object Object]"},"Childcare interruptions create productivity pressure, but career visibility concerns may be the more serious long-term risk."],"\n",["LI",{"class":"leading-[150%]","node":"[object Object]"},"Expecting parents and parents already caring for young children require different forms of employer support."],"\n",["LI",{"class":"leading-[150%]","node":"[object Object]"},"Parents with limited access to paid or family childcare experience greater workplace friction."],"\n"],"\n"],"\n",["LI",{"class":"leading-[150%]","node":"[object Object]"},"\n",["P",{"class":"mb-3","node":"[object Object]"},["STRONG",{"class":"font-bold text-[#464646]","node":"[object Object]"},"KPIs to report:"]],"\n",["UL",{"class":"list-disc pl-5 mb-3 flex flex-col gap-1","node":"[object Object]"},"\n",["LI",{"class":"leading-[150%]","node":"[object Object]"},"Percentage experiencing each pain point frequently."],"\n",["LI",{"class":"leading-[150%]","node":"[object Object]"},"Average severity score by pain-point area."],"\n",["LI",{"class":"leading-[150%]","node":"[object Object]"},"Current-versus-preferred work arrangement gap."],"\n",["LI",{"class":"leading-[150%]","node":"[object Object]"},"Percentage reporting low control over working hours."],"\n",["LI",{"class":"leading-[150%]","node":"[object Object]"},"Percentage uncomfortable requesting flexibility."],"\n",["LI",{"class":"leading-[150%]","node":"[object Object]"},"Percentage reporting career visibility or progression concerns."],"\n",["LI",{"class":"leading-[150%]","node":"[object Object]"},"Awareness, access, usefulness, and unmet need for existing employer support."],"\n",["LI",{"class":"leading-[150%]","node":"[object Object]"},"Priority share for each proposed policy or support action."],"\n",["LI",{"class":"leading-[150%]","node":"[object Object]"},"Top-ranked urgent problem to solve."],"\n",["LI",{"class":"leading-[150%]","node":"[object Object]"},"Qualitative themes from the open-ended parent experience responses."],"\n"],"\n"],"\n"]]]]]]]]]]]]]],["DIV",{"class":"flex flex-col w-full overflow-x-visible"},[[205,555]],["DIV",{"class":"flex w-full justify-start items-start flex-col mt-[8px] h-[24px] relative overflow-visible","style":"opacity: 1; transform: none;"},["DIV",{"class":"absolute inset-0 flex flex-col justify-between items-start pointer-events-none","style":"opacity: 1;"},["DIV",{"class":"flex items-center gap-[4px] -ml-[5px] pointer-events-auto"},[[205,557]],["BUTTON",{"class":"relative group flex items-center justify-center w-[24px] h-[24px] rounded-[8px] overflow-visible opacity-40 cursor-not-allowed","disabled":""},["SPAN",{"aria-hidden":"true","class":"flex-shrink-0 bg-[#808080] transition-colors duration-200 ","style":"width: 14px; height: 14px; mask-image: url(\"/icons/retry_2.svg\"); mask-size: contain; mask-repeat: no-repeat; mask-position: center center;"}]]]]],[[205,566]]]]]]]],[[7,501]],["DIV",{"class":"flex justify-start pointer-events-auto  w-full"},["DIV",{"class":"flex flex-col w-[96%] mx-[2%]"},[[103,486]],["DIV",{"class":"flex w-full "},["DIV",{"class":"flex rounded-[8px] bg-transparent text-[#464646] w-full flex-shri